{
  "case_id": "2006-06-6407",
  "document_hash": "889ed7a6fc8f92ef4ff9afddb4ca211c0c410437e448d2e7d673a3e28805372b",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-06-6407",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "889ed7a6fc8f92ef4ff9afddb4ca211c0c410437e448d2e7d673a3e28805372b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-889ed7a6fc8f-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 1:00 p.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2006-06-6407",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "889ed7a6fc8f92ef4ff9afddb4ca211c0c410437e448d2e7d673a3e28805372b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-889ed7a6fc8f-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Fifth Circuit found that Scott Panetti suffers from paranoid delusions that cause him to believe that he is being executed because of a conspiracy against him and not as punishment for his crimes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-06-6407",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "889ed7a6fc8f92ef4ff9afddb4ca211c0c410437e448d2e7d673a3e28805372b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-889ed7a6fc8f-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Wait. I didn't understand that to be what the case said. I thought that the case held that it wasn't successive there because the claim had, in fact, been brought in the first petition, and that first petition was dismissed as premature."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-06-6407",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "889ed7a6fc8f92ef4ff9afddb4ca211c0c410437e448d2e7d673a3e28805372b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-889ed7a6fc8f-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Here, how do you get around the language other than to say it shouldn't be that way, that you should be able to bring a second or successive petition when you're raising an issue that was not ripe at the time of the first petition?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-06-6407",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "889ed7a6fc8f92ef4ff9afddb4ca211c0c410437e448d2e7d673a3e28805372b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-889ed7a6fc8f-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is it material to your position to show that there was deterioration in his mental condition between the time of the sentence and the time you brought the petition?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2006-06-6407",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "889ed7a6fc8f92ef4ff9afddb4ca211c0c410437e448d2e7d673a3e28805372b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-889ed7a6fc8f-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But our contention is that the AEDPA does not prevent this Court from addressing the merits of the constitutional issue here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-06-6407",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "889ed7a6fc8f92ef4ff9afddb4ca211c0c410437e448d2e7d673a3e28805372b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-889ed7a6fc8f-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well does he understand why he's being imprisoned? I mean, does this, the Ford right extend to prison? Is it cruel to keep someone locked up for life when they don't understand why they're being locked up for life?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Wiercich (Respondent)",
      "case_id": "2006-06-6407",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "889ed7a6fc8f92ef4ff9afddb4ca211c0c410437e448d2e7d673a3e28805372b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-889ed7a6fc8f-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think that's the very nature of the Ford right, that it is something that intervenes. We're not saying that Scott Panetti was not fully culpable, found guilty, sentenced to death; we're not attacking that at all. Something happened. And what happened was he did lose the ability to understand rationally the connection between his crime --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-06-6407",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "889ed7a6fc8f92ef4ff9afddb4ca211c0c410437e448d2e7d673a3e28805372b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-889ed7a6fc8f-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You mean we can't predict that the delusion today is the same delusion yesterday?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Cruz (Respondent)",
      "case_id": "2006-06-6407",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "889ed7a6fc8f92ef4ff9afddb4ca211c0c410437e448d2e7d673a3e28805372b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-889ed7a6fc8f-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For centuries courts have struggled with how to reconcile mental illness with criminal justice. In this case, however, the court should not reach the merits of that issue because the AEDPA presents two independent jurisdictional bars to reaching the merits. First, Section 2254 bars relief because the State court proceedings complied with clearly established law under Ford; and second, the plain text of Section 2244 bars relief because Panetti's claim was a second or successive habeas application."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-06-6407",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "889ed7a6fc8f92ef4ff9afddb4ca211c0c410437e448d2e7d673a3e28805372b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-889ed7a6fc8f-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "indication from those two exceptions that Congress simply wasn't adverting to this problem?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-06-6407",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "889ed7a6fc8f92ef4ff9afddb4ca211c0c410437e448d2e7d673a3e28805372b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-889ed7a6fc8f-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is that constitutional?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-06-6407",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "889ed7a6fc8f92ef4ff9afddb4ca211c0c410437e448d2e7d673a3e28805372b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-889ed7a6fc8f-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What about that one?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Cruz",
      "case_id": "2006-06-6407",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "889ed7a6fc8f92ef4ff9afddb4ca211c0c410437e448d2e7d673a3e28805372b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-889ed7a6fc8f-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In this case, Panetti satisfies that test."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-06-6407",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "889ed7a6fc8f92ef4ff9afddb4ca211c0c410437e448d2e7d673a3e28805372b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-889ed7a6fc8f-0002-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The district court found that Panetti understands he committed these two murders. He knows that he murdered two people. He understand that he is going to be put to death."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-06-6407",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "889ed7a6fc8f92ef4ff9afddb4ca211c0c410437e448d2e7d673a3e28805372b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-889ed7a6fc8f-0002-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Panetti knows he's going to die and he also knows he's guilty."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2006-06-6407",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "889ed7a6fc8f92ef4ff9afddb4ca211c0c410437e448d2e7d673a3e28805372b",
